{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"parser","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parser"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/markdown/parser"},{"type":"text","value":" entry exports only the document parser and its transitive implementation."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { parseMarkdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/parser'","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parsemarkdown","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parseMarkdown"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function parseMarkdown(\n  markdown: string,\n  options?: ParseOptions,\n): MarkdownDocument","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Normalizes and parses a complete Markdown source string into a deterministic "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MarkdownDocument"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Behavior"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"allowHtml"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recognize raw block and inline HTML nodes"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"urlTransform"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"built-in policy"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Override parsed link and image URLs; see "},{"type":"link","href":"../core-concepts/security.md#custom-url-policy","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom URL policy"}]}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"frontmatter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Extract a leading "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"---"},{"type":"text","value":" frontmatter block"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"headingIds"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generate IDs, disable them, or provide an ID function"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"extensions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[]"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run custom parser and transform hooks in array order"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"references"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"internal"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provide normalized reference definitions to nested parsing"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"footnotes"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"internal"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provide normalized footnote definitions to nested parsing"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"footnoteOrder"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"internal"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Track first-reference order through nested parsing"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"footnoteCounts"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"internal"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Track repeated references for back links"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The last four state fields are public so extension-driven nested parsing can preserve parser context. Ordinary calls should leave them unset."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"result","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Result"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The result always has "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"type: 'root'"},{"type":"text","value":" and a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"children"},{"type":"text","value":" array. It may also include raw "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"frontmatter"},{"type":"text","value":" and extension-derived "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"headings"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"../core-concepts/parsing.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parsing"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for behavior and "},{"type":"link","href":"./types.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Types"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for complete contracts."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"parser","text":"Parser","level":1},{"id":"parsemarkdown","text":"parseMarkdown","level":2},{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":3},{"id":"result","text":"Result","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n# Parser\n\nThe `@tanstack/markdown/parser` entry exports only the document parser and its transitive implementation.\n\n```ts\nimport { parseMarkdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/parser'\n```\n\n## `parseMarkdown`\n\n```ts\nfunction parseMarkdown(\n  markdown: string,\n  options?: ParseOptions,\n): MarkdownDocument\n```\n\nNormalizes and parses a complete Markdown source string into a deterministic `MarkdownDocument`.\n\n### Options\n\n| Option | Default | Behavior |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `allowHtml` | `false` | Recognize raw block and inline HTML nodes |\n| `urlTransform` | built-in policy | Override parsed link and image URLs; see [Custom URL policy](../core-concepts/security.md#custom-url-policy) |\n| `frontmatter` | `true` | Extract a leading `---` frontmatter block |\n| `headingIds` | `true` | Generate IDs, disable them, or provide an ID function |\n| `extensions` | `[]` | Run custom parser and transform hooks in array order |\n| `references` | internal | Provide normalized reference definitions to nested parsing |\n| `footnotes` | internal | Provide normalized footnote definitions to nested parsing |\n| `footnoteOrder` | internal | Track first-reference order through nested parsing |\n| `footnoteCounts` | internal | Track repeated references for back links |\n\nThe last four state fields are public so extension-driven nested parsing can preserve parser context. Ordinary calls should leave them unset.\n\n### Result\n\nThe result always has `type: 'root'` and a `children` array. It may also include raw `frontmatter` and extension-derived `headings`.\n\nSee [Parsing](../core-concepts/parsing.md) for behavior and [Types](./types.md) for complete contracts.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Parser\n---\n\n# Parser\n\nThe `@tanstack/markdown/parser` entry exports only the document parser and its transitive implementation.\n\n```ts\nimport { parseMarkdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/parser'\n```\n\n## `parseMarkdown`\n\n```ts\nfunction parseMarkdown(\n  markdown: string,\n  options?: ParseOptions,\n): MarkdownDocument\n```\n\nNormalizes and parses a complete Markdown source string into a deterministic `MarkdownDocument`.\n\n### Options\n\n| Option | Default | Behavior |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `allowHtml` | `false` | Recognize raw block and inline HTML nodes |\n| `urlTransform` | built-in policy | Override parsed link and image URLs; see [Custom URL policy](../core-concepts/security.md#custom-url-policy) |\n| `frontmatter` | `true` | Extract a leading `---` frontmatter block |\n| `headingIds` | `true` | Generate IDs, disable them, or provide an ID function |\n| `extensions` | `[]` | Run custom parser and transform hooks in array order |\n| `references` | internal | Provide normalized reference definitions to nested parsing |\n| `footnotes` | internal | Provide normalized footnote definitions to nested parsing |\n| `footnoteOrder` | internal | Track first-reference order through nested parsing |\n| `footnoteCounts` | internal | Track repeated references for back links |\n\nThe last four state fields are public so extension-driven nested parsing can preserve parser context. Ordinary calls should leave them unset.\n\n### Result\n\nThe result always has `type: 'root'` and a `children` array. It may also include raw `frontmatter` and extension-derived `headings`.\n\nSee [Parsing](../core-concepts/parsing.md) for behavior and [Types](./types.md) for complete contracts.\n"}
